Assuming the package is already installed (the affy package will also 
install missing packages from BioC), all you really need is something like:

require(thepackagename, quietly = TRUE, character.only = TRUE) ||
stop(paste("The package", thepackagename, "needs to be installed first."))

There is quite a bit of other code in the affy package for automatic 
loading of packages, but the use case there is much more complicated.

