Hi Richard,

If you can get R installed and running on your computer, then by 
definition most of the Bioconductor packages will 'run' as well. The 
only caveat being that some packages rely on non-R software for some of 
their functionality, and if that software isn't installed (or 
installable), then you won't be able to use that particular package.

However it is more likely that a package will work on a Linux variant 
rather than Mac OS or Windows.

Best,

Jim



