From: oliveros at cnb.uam.es (Juan C Oliveros Collazos)
Date: Fri, 30 Nov 2007 12:39:50 +0100
Subject: [BioC] New on-line tool to view microarray results
Message-ID: <474FF686.9080508@cnb.uam.es>

Dear all,

Users of Bioconductor packages that obtain their microarray results as 
expression tables may be interested in our tool:

FIESTA Viewer:

http://bioinfogp.cnb.csic.es/tools/FIESTA

On-line tool for visualizing microarray results obtained in comparative 
experiments with replicates.


Main features:

-Free

-Transforms a simple table of results into interactive web pages 
containing interactive plots, search engines, external links, etc.

-Compatible with virtually any statistical method used (the system 
accepts any text-tabulated file containing pvalues, logRatios, 
logIntensities, Gene descriptions...).

-Compatible with any operative system (it is an on-line tool)

-The results are provided as standard web pages. You can visualize them 
on-line or download them to your hard disk.


Feel free to use it with your data or with the example provided. Please 
report us any problem or comment.

FIESTA Viewer will be demonstrated at the:

"Critical Assessment of Microarray Data Analysis" CAMDA07
(Valencia, Spain, 12-14 December, 2007)
http://camda.bioinfo.cipf.es/index.html

Try other BioinfoGP tools at:
http://bioinfogp.cnb.csic.es/tools

All the Best!

Juan Carlos Oliveros
BioinfoGP, CNB-CSIC


